      "writtenOn": "2023-06-09T15:58:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The drivers that use the \"device_for_each_child\" function are \"rpmsg_ctrl\" and \"rpmsg_char,\" and these two drivers are not maintained by us.\nSource code files:\n\ndrivers/rpmsg/rpmsg_char.c\ndrivers/rpmsg/rpmsg_ctrl.c\n\nAdditionally, the usage of \"driver_for_each_device\" and \"bus_for_each_dev\" is demonstrated as follows:\n``` \nstatic void __exit rtk_hdmi_exit(void)\n{\n\tint err;\n\n\terr \u003d driver_for_each_device(\u0026rtk_hdmi_driver.driver,\n\t\t\tNULL, NULL, rtk_hdmi_exit_callback);\n\tif (err)\n\t\tpr_err(\"%s fail\", __func__);\n\n\tplatform_driver_unregister(\u0026rtk_hdmi_driver);\n}\n\nmodule_exit(rtk_hdmi_exit);\n``` \n-----\n```\nstatic int __optee_unregister_device(struct device *dev, void *data)\n{\n\tif (!strncmp(dev_name(dev), \"optee-ta\", strlen(\"optee-ta\")))\n\t\tdevice_unregister(dev);\n\n\treturn 0;\n}\n\nvoid optee_unregister_devices(void)\n{\n\tbus_for_each_dev(\u0026tee_bus_type, NULL, NULL,\n\t\t\t __optee_unregister_device);\n}\n```",
